@issyl0 Sorry for confusion. My thinking is aligning formulae and casks on how audits work. Formulae do not have the concept of non-fatal warnings: something is either an audit failure or it is not displayed. `brew audit` is the typical flow, `brew audit --strict` displays optional audit failures.

As a result, I propose that all current cask audit warnings are never displayed as warnings but the underlying audit checks turned into errors displayed only with `--strict` (or one of the other relevant flags).

Does that make more sense?
